---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Project Vanguard — Apple InfoSec Case Study • Tushar Roy">
	<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#faf8f2] text-[#1a1918] antialiased selection:bg-black selection:text-white">
		<!-- Top Progress & Return Bar -->
		<header class="sticky top-0 z-40 bg-[#faf8f2]/95 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-black/15 py-3.5 px-6">
			<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto flex items-center justify-between font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
				<a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-black hover:text-neutral-600 transition-colors no-underline">
					<span>←</span>
					<span>Selected Works</span>
				</a>
				<div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-black/60 hidden sm:flex">
					<span>Apple InfoSec</span>
					<span>•</span>
					<span class="text-black font-bold">Project Vanguard</span>
					<span>•</span>
					<span>Staff Product Designer</span>
				</div>
				<a href="#section-11" class="px-3 py-1 bg-black text-white hover:bg-neutral-800 transition-colors no-underline text-[11px]">
					Key Takeaways ↓
				</a>
			</div>
		</header>

		<!-- Case Study Main Container -->
		<main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-28">

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 0: HERO & OVERVIEW                            -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="mb-24 md:mb-32 border-b border-black/15 pb-20">
				<!-- Kicker -->
				<span class="font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#8c827a] block mb-3 font-semibold">
					Apple InfoSec · Staff Product Designer
				</span>

				<!-- Heading -->
				<h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-[54px] font-bold text-black mb-8 leading-[1.08] tracking-tight">
					The security metrics platform that told executives how much to trust each number
				</h1>

				<!-- Text -->
				<div class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-black/85 leading-relaxed space-y-5 max-w-3xl mb-10">
					<p>
						Apple InfoSec ran on a <strong>small BI team</strong> that hand-built metrics for every partner team. Coverage sat <strong>under 30%</strong>. Getting one new metric published took about <strong>two months</strong>. By the time a metric went live, it was often stale.
					</p>
					<p>
						That left senior executives without a <strong>quantitative answer</strong> to the one question that mattered: how well are we keeping Apple safe? In board-level conversations they were using <strong>thumbs-up and thumbs-down emojis</strong>.
					</p>
					<p>
						I replaced the static reporting site with a <strong>governed self-service intelligence platform</strong>. Every metric on it carries a <strong>visible trust level</strong>.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Project Meta Box -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 bg-white border border-black/15 p-6 mb-12 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000] font-departure text-xs">
					<div>
						<span class="text-black/50 block uppercase mb-1">Role</span>
						<strong class="font-bold text-black text-sm block">Staff Product Designer</strong>
						<span class="text-black/70 mt-1 block">Strategy, interaction model, governance design.</span>
					</div>
					<div>
						<span class="text-black/50 block uppercase mb-1">Collaborating Teams</span>
						<strong class="font-bold text-black text-sm block">InfoSec BI & Data Eng</strong>
						<span class="text-black/70 mt-1 block">Incident management, 30+ partner security orgs.</span>
					</div>
					<div>
						<span class="text-black/50 block uppercase mb-1">Confidentiality Note</span>
						<strong class="font-bold text-black text-sm block">Illustrative Data</strong>
						<span class="text-black/70 mt-1 block">All numbers and screens shown here are reconstructed. No confidential Apple data is included.</span>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- ARTIFACT 01: Hero Before & After Image -->
				<div class="border-2 border-black bg-white p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-[5px_5px_0_0_#000] mb-3">
					<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 items-stretch">
						<!-- Left: Old Static Dashboard -->
						<div class="md:col-span-4 bg-[#f4f2eb] border border-black/20 p-4 flex flex-col justify-between">
							<div>
								<div class="flex items-center justify-between font-departure text-[10px] uppercase text-black/50 pb-2 mb-3 border-b border-black/10">
									<span>BEFORE (2024)</span>
									<span class="text-red-700 font-bold">28% COVERAGE</span>
								</div>
								<div class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-black mb-2">Internal Security Wiki Table</div>
								<p class="font-sans text-xs text-black/70 leading-normal mb-4">
									Static HTML tables updated manually via spreadsheets. No data lineage, stale quarterly reviews, and subjective status indicators.
								</p>
								<div class="space-y-2 font-mono text-[11px] bg-white p-3 border border-black/10">
									<div class="flex justify-between items-center pb-1.5 border-b border-black/5">
										<span class="text-black/60">MTTD Endpoint:</span>
										<span class="font-bold">👍 Nominal</span>
									</div>
									<div class="flex justify-between items-center pb-1.5 border-b border-black/5">
										<span class="text-black/60">Cloud IAM Drift:</span>
										<span class="font-bold">👎 At Risk</span>
									</div>
									<div class="flex justify-between items-center">
										<span class="text-black/60">Audit SLA:</span>
										<span class="text-black/40 italic">Stale (Q2)</span>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-black/10 font-departure text-[10px] text-black/50 text-center">
								Subjective emoji reporting • No lineage
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- Right: New Vanguard Platform Overview -->
						<div class="md:col-span-8 bg-neutral-900 border border-black overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between">
							<div class="relative group">
								<img
									src="/images/case-study/vanguard/platform-overview.png"
									alt="Project Vanguard Platform Overview"
									class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
								/>
								<div class="absolute top-3 right-3 bg-black/80 text-white font-departure text-[10px] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-white/20 backdrop-blur">
									SHIPPED PLATFORM // 85%+ COVERAGE
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<!-- Caption -->
				<figcaption class="font-departure text-xs text-black/60 uppercase tracking-wider block">
					Caption: Before and after. The change people notice first is the badge on every metric.
				</figcaption>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 1: THE PROBLEM                                -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="mb-24 md:mb-32 border-b border-black/15 pb-20">
				<!-- Kicker -->
				<span class="font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#8c827a] block mb-3 font-semibold">
					The problem
				</span>

				<!-- Heading -->
				<h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-black mb-6 leading-tight">
					Executives had no defensible way to answer "are we safe?"
				</h2>

				<!-- Text -->
				<div class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-black/85 leading-relaxed space-y-5 max-w-3xl mb-10">
					<p>
						The BI team was the <strong>only path</strong> to a published metric. A request moved through four steps. Define the measure. Negotiate the formula. Chase data engineering. Publish. Average time was <strong>two months</strong>.
					</p>
					<p>
						Because the queue was slow, teams stopped waiting. They <strong>built their own dashboards</strong>. Those dashboards held real metrics that never entered the central platform. So executives now had two problems instead of one. The central view was <strong>incomplete</strong>, and the numbers they heard in meetings <strong>did not match</strong> the numbers on the platform.
					</p>
					<p>
						When a metric spiked, an executive had no way to check it themselves. They picked up the phone. That started a chain of <strong>formal and informal assurance calls</strong> across teams, repeated for every stakeholder who asked.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- ARTIFACT 02: Diagram -->
				<div class="border-2 border-black bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-[5px_5px_0_0_#000] mb-3">
					<div class="font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-black/60 pb-3 mb-6 border-b border-black/15 flex justify-between items-center">
						<span>LEGACY WORKFLOW & SHADOW DASHBOARD FRAGMENTATION</span>
						<span class="text-red-700 font-bold">BOTTLENECK: ~2 MONTHS</span>
					</div>

					<!-- Visual Workflow Diagram -->
					<div class="space-y-6">
						<!-- Main 4-step linear chain -->
						<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 relative">
							<div class="border border-black p-4 bg-[#faf8f2]">
								<div class="font-departure text-[10px] text-black/50 mb-1">STEP 01</div>
								<div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-black">Define Measure</div>
								<div class="font-sans text-xs text-black/60 mt-1">Partner org drafts requirement</div>
							</div>
							<div class="border-2 border-red-700 p-4 bg-red-50/50">
								<div class="font-departure text-[10px] text-red-700 font-bold mb-1">STEP 02 (CHOKEPOINT)</div>
								<div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-black">Negotiate Formula</div>
								<div class="font-sans text-xs text-black/60 mt-1">Multi-week committee debates</div>
							</div>
							<div class="border border-black p-4 bg-[#faf8f2]">
								<div class="font-departure text-[10px] text-black/50 mb-1">STEP 03</div>
								<div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-black">Chase Data Eng</div>
								<div class="font-sans text-xs text-black/60 mt-1">Pipeline backlog prioritization</div>
							</div>
							<div class="border border-black p-4 bg-[#faf8f2]">
								<div class="font-departure text-[10px] text-black/50 mb-1">STEP 04</div>
								<div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-black">Publish Central</div>
								<div class="font-sans text-xs text-black/60 mt-1">Stale on arrival (Day ~60)</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- Branch to Shadow Dashboards -->
						<div class="border-l-2 border-dashed border-red-600 pl-6 ml-12 sm:ml-48 py-2">
							<div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-300 p-4 rounded-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-3">
								<div>
									<div class="font-departure text-xs text-red-800 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
										<span>↳ Teams Peel Off:</span>
										<span>Proliferation of Shadow Dashboards</span>
									</div>
									<p class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 mt-1 m-0">
										Unvetted spreadsheets, rogue Grafana instances, and conflicting numbers in leadership meetings.
									</p>
								</div>
								<span class="font-departure text-[11px] bg-red-200/80 text-red-900 px-3 py-1 font-bold whitespace-nowrap self-start sm:self-auto">
									CONFIDENCE = 0
								</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<!-- Caption -->
				<figcaption class="font-departure text-xs text-black/60 uppercase tracking-wider block">
					Caption: Slow onboarding did not just delay metrics. It pushed teams to build in the dark.
				</figcaption>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 2: RESEARCH                                   -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="mb-24 md:mb-32 border-b border-black/15 pb-20">
				<!-- Kicker -->
				<span class="font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#8c827a] block mb-3 font-semibold">
					Research
				</span>

				<!-- Heading -->
				<h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-black mb-6 leading-tight">
					I went to the people who author metrics and the people who read them
				</h2>

				<!-- Text -->
				<div class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-black/85 leading-relaxed space-y-5 max-w-3xl mb-10">
					<p>
						I started with a <strong>design sprint</strong> with the BI team to map how a metric actually gets made. Then I ran interviews on both ends of the pipe. <strong>Six metric authors</strong> from partner security orgs. <strong>Two executives</strong> who consume the output.
					</p>
					<p>
						The authors told me the bottleneck was <strong>negotiation</strong>, not effort. They knew their own data. They were waiting on someone else to agree on a formula.
					</p>
					<p>
						The executives told me something I did not expect. Their problem was not missing data. It was <strong>not knowing which numbers were solid</strong>. They had learned to discount anything they could not trace.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- ARTIFACT 03: Research Summary Board -->
				<div class="border-2 border-black bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-[5px_5px_0_0_#000] mb-3">
					<div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-8">
						<!-- Left: Design Sprint Output -->
						<div class="md:col-span-5 bg-[#faf8f2] border border-black/20 p-5">
							<div class="font-departure text-xs uppercase text-black/60 font-bold mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-black/10">
								DESIGN SPRINT MAPPING // BI TEAM
							</div>
							<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-black mb-2">Process Bottleneck Analysis</h4>
							<p class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
								Mapping the 5-conversation handoff cycle revealed that 70% of BI engineering time was spent mediating disputes rather than instrumenting feeds.
							</p>
							<div class="space-y-2 font-departure text-xs">
								<div class="bg-white p-2.5 border border-black/10">
									<strong class="block text-black">6 Metric Authors</strong>
									<span class="text-black/60 text-[11px]">Partner orgs (Cloud, Identity, Endpoint)</span>
								</div>
								<div class="bg-white p-2.5 border border-black/10">
									<strong class="block text-black">2 Senior Executives</strong>
									<span class="text-black/60 text-[11px]">C-suite & VP of InfoSec Assurance</span>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- Right: Grouped Interview Quotes -->
						<div class="md:col-span-7 space-y-4">
							<div class="border border-black p-4 bg-white">
								<div class="font-departure text-[11px] uppercase text-[#8c827a] font-bold mb-1">
									AUTHOR PAIN: SPEED & AUTONOMY
								</div>
								<blockquote class="font-serif italic text-sm text-black leading-relaxed m-0 border-l-2 border-black pl-3">
									"We know our telemetry cold. The bottleneck isn't getting the logs—it's waiting two months for a central team to approve our denominator."
								</blockquote>
							</div>

							<div class="border border-black p-4 bg-white">
								<div class="font-departure text-[11px] uppercase text-[#8c827a] font-bold mb-1">
									EXECUTIVE PAIN: TRUST & TRACEABILITY
								</div>
								<blockquote class="font-serif italic text-sm text-black leading-relaxed m-0 border-l-2 border-black pl-3">
									"Our problem isn't that numbers are missing. It's that we have no idea which numbers are rock solid, so we discount everything we can't trace back to source."
								</blockquote>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<!-- Caption -->
				<figcaption class="font-departure text-xs text-black/60 uppercase tracking-wider block">
					Caption: Two groups, two different problems. Speed for authors. Confidence for executives.
				</figcaption>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 3: STRATEGY                                   -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="mb-24 md:mb-32 border-b border-black/15 pb-20">
				<!-- Kicker -->
				<span class="font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#8c827a] block mb-3 font-semibold">
					Strategy
				</span>

				<!-- Heading -->
				<h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-black mb-6 leading-tight">
					The team had two plans. I argued for one.
				</h2>

				<!-- Text -->
				<div class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-black/85 leading-relaxed space-y-5 max-w-3xl mb-10">
					<p>
						When I joined, the team had already split the work into <strong>two separate tracks</strong>. Track one was to standardize and speed up metric onboarding. Track two was to build a <strong>security impact framework</strong> that answered the executive question directly.
					</p>
					<p>
						I argued for a <strong>single solution: self-service</strong>.
					</p>
					<p>
						My reasoning was simple. If each team can onboard its own metrics, then <strong>each team's own clarity and speed decides its coverage</strong>. The BI queue stops being the limit. And once a team has that autonomy, it has <strong>no reason to spin up a shadow dashboard</strong>.
					</p>
					<p>
						There was a second win. A self-service platform <strong>generates its own usage data</strong>. That gave the BI team quantitative evidence to show their own leadership, who were also their customers.
					</p>
					<p>
						I got buy-in by showing that track two was a <strong>reporting layer on top of track one</strong>. It could not exist without coverage, and coverage could not exist without speed.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- ARTIFACT 04: Strategy Diagram -->
				<div class="border-2 border-black bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-[5px_5px_0_0_#000] mb-3">
					<div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center">
						<!-- Left: Two Competing Tracks -->
						<div class="md:col-span-5 space-y-3">
							<div class="font-departure text-xs uppercase text-black/50 font-bold mb-2">ORIGINAL 2-TRACK PROPOSAL</div>
							<div class="border border-black/30 p-3 bg-neutral-50 text-xs">
								<strong class="block font-bold">Track 01: Central Onboarding Speed</strong>
								<span class="text-black/60 text-[11px]">Optimize the internal BI queue</span>
							</div>
							<div class="text-center font-departure text-xs text-red-600 font-bold">VS (COMPETING FOR ENG TIME)</div>
							<div class="border border-black/30 p-3 bg-neutral-50 text-xs">
								<strong class="block font-bold">Track 02: Security Impact Model</strong>
								<span class="text-black/60 text-[11px]">Separate executive reporting layer</span>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- Center Arrow -->
						<div class="md:col-span-2 text-center font-departure text-2xl font-bold text-black hidden md:block">
							→
						</div>

						<!-- Right: Collapsed Single Solution & 3 Effects -->
						<div class="md:col-span-5 bg-[#faf8f2] border-2 border-black p-5 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000]">
							<div class="font-departure text-[11px] text-emerald-800 uppercase font-bold mb-2">SHIPPED ARCHITECTURE</div>
							<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-lg text-black mb-3">Single Self-Service Platform</h4>
							<div class="space-y-2.5 font-departure text-xs">
								<div class="bg-white p-2 border border-black/10 flex items-center gap-2">
									<span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold">01</span>
									<span>Coverage: Speed in hands of authors</span>
								</div>
								<div class="bg-white p-2 border border-black/10 flex items-center gap-2">
									<span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold">02</span>
									<span>Shadow Dashboards Eliminated</span>
								</div>
								<div class="bg-white p-2 border border-black/10 flex items-center gap-2">
									<span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold">03</span>
									<span>Auto-Generated Usage Telemetry</span>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<!-- Caption -->
				<figcaption class="font-departure text-xs text-black/60 uppercase tracking-wider block">
					Caption: One solution fed all three goals. Two solutions would have competed for the same engineering time.
				</figcaption>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 4: THE HARD PROBLEM                           -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="mb-24 md:mb-32 border-b border-black/15 pb-20">
				<!-- Kicker -->
				<span class="font-departure text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#8c827a] block mb-3 font-semibold">
					The hard problem
				</span>

				<!-- Heading -->
				<h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-black mb-6 leading-tight">
					Self-service creates a new risk, and the risk is trust
				</h2>

				<!-- Text -->
				<div class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-black/85 leading-relaxed space-y-5 max-w-3xl mb-10">
					<p>
						The moment anyone can publish a metric, every metric stops being equal. A metric vetted by the BI team and a metric published by a partner team on a Friday afternoon would sit on the same page, in the same card, at the same size.
					</p>
					<p>
						So the executive question changed. It moved from <strong>"where is the number?"</strong> to <strong>"how much can I trust this number?"</strong>
					</p>
					<p>
						That became my core design problem. Make the <strong>trust level visible</strong> on every metric, at every level of the interface.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- ARTIFACT 05: Annotated Metric Card -->
				<div class="border-2 border-black bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-[5px_5px_0_0_#000] mb-3">
					<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
						<!-- Card Preview -->
						<div class="border-2 border-black bg-[#faf8f2] p-6 shadow-[4px_4px_0_0_#000] relative">
							<!-- Header with Badge & Owner Callouts -->
							<div class="flex items-start justify-between pb-4 mb-4 border-b border-black/15">
								<div>
									<div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
										<span class="font-departure text-[11px] text-black/60 uppercase">SECOPS-INCIDENT-01</span>
										<!-- CALLOUT 1: TRUST BADGE -->
										<span class="relative inline-flex items-center gap-1 bg-black text-white px-2 py-0.5 font-departure text-[10px] font-bold uppercase rounded-sm">
											<span>●</span>
											<span>VETTED</span>
										</span>
									</div>
									<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-black m-0">Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)</h3>
								</div>
								<!-- CALLOUT 2: FRESHNESS -->
								<div class="text-right font-departure text-[11px] text-black/60">
									<span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold block">● FRESH</span>
									<span>Synced 4h ago</span>
								</div>
							</div>

							<!-- Metric Stat & Trend -->
							<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-4">
								<div>
									<div class="font-departure text-xs text-black/50 uppercase">Current Window</div>
									<div class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-black mt-1">4.9 Hours</div>
									<div class="font-departure text-xs text-emerald-700 font-bold mt-1">↓ -18% vs Baseline</div>
								</div>
								<div class="border border-black/15 bg-white p-3 font-mono text-[11px] space-y-1">
									<div class="flex justify-between text-black/60">
										<span>Target:</span>
										<strong class="text-black">&lt; 6.0h</strong>
									</div>
									<div class="flex justify-between text-black/60">
										<span>Control Limits:</span>
